Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.230 align:start position:0%
 
distinguished guests  it is an honor for me to be once again a  patron of the world health summit  you might remember when we met one year  ago i told you about the first steps  that we had taken  to increase cooperation inside europe  the world was called off guard by covet  19.  no country was truly prepared  to tackle a health emergency on this  scale  one year ago we didn't even know whether  a safe and effective vaccine  would be available  we had to learn how to scale up vaccine  production  and we had to implement the largest  vaccine program ever  today  more than 75 percent of adults in the  european union are fully vaccinated  we have delivered more than  850 million doses to european citizens  and in parallel  we have shipped more than one billion  doses to the rest of the world  we were the only region to do that  i promise that every second dose  produced in europe  will be exported  and we kept that promise and delivered  to 150 countries so far  so this was european solidarity at its  best  and there's a second success story  thanks to the european digital covet  certificate  travel is possible again  43 countries from four continents locked  into our digital certificate  and 27 more are lining up to join  but we are not out of the woods yet  the year since we last saw each other  has been unbelievable hard  and at the same time it has been very  enlightening and incredibly productive  politicians and the public have  understood that  national solutions alone are not enough  to fight a pandemic  and even more importantly  we have understood  that mutual preparedness is everything  in a global health crisis  the european union drew its lessons and  acted we have created a new health  emergency preparedness and response  authority  in short hera  hera's task is to better prepare for  health emergencies  to detect them promptly  and to respond collectively  its scope  reaches from the collective procurement  of protective equipment for example  medicines and vaccines  to coordinating the rules for testing  and quarantine  hera is ready to launch early next year  now what are the tasks of this new  authority  in normal times  we call this the preparedness phase  in normal times hero will work to assess  health threats  for example to detect them at an early  stage including by innovative methods  for instance today we can predict the  spread of covet 19 in a community by  monitoring the wastewater  so here i will invest in that  in sharing data throughout the new  european health data space  and in assessing new and emerging  biological threats  such as those connected for example to  the melting of permafrost  or the destruction of biodiversity  or take the increasing threat of  anti-microbial resistance  while the world is still focused on  fighting covet 19  this risk is progressing silently  and if our medicines do not work anymore  many lives will be lost  but we need to see even further  bioterrorism  or the unintentional release of  pathogens are real scenarios that  require better preparedness as well  hera will make use of all the available  knowledge and intelligence  and hera's task is to identify threats  early on  to might make sure  that we have the necessary medical  counter measures available  hera will be a watchtower safeguarding  public health  now in crisis times  here i will be given special powers  for instance to coordinate action with  our member states through a health  crisis board  because we need fast and decisive  decision making  or for example to procure medical  equipment medicines vaccines  or even critical raw materials  just to tackle the crisis  hera will support the development of  state-of-the-art diagnostics  that can be readily modified  but also high-end medical devices  such as for example the next generation  of portable ventilators  and hera will work on new flexible  technologies for even better vaccines so  you all know the demand is huge  hera will help to bridge gaps in the  existing european health system and to  take cooperation to a new level  let me give you some examples  it will work on pan-european clinical  trials  it will create a network of european  production sites  for critical medical countermeasures  which then can be activated quickly in  case of emergency  and it will work with private companies  to address the bottlenecks in our supply  chains  in early 2022 we will launch  work on ever-ready industrial production  capacities  so to manufacture vaccines and medicines  rapidly in case of a crisis  and finally i don't need to explain to  you that global cooperation is  vital  cross-border health threats need  cross-border responses  so here as horizon will be wider than  our union  another of hera's core tasks  will be to join forces  with its international counterparts  we have already started to build bridges  to the work of the who  and of barda in the united states  we are in contact with third countries  in our neighborhood  such as the united kingdom switzerlands  and the western balkan countries  our aim is to form a core group  that will lead to a truly global network  of heroes  and more will come with the african cdc  with the future african medicines agency  and of course with other global players  such as seppi garvey and the  philanthropic foundations  beyond such cooperation i am convinced  that we need a global standard for  health preparedness  and this is why i organized together  with the g20 the global health summit in  rome earlier this year  with the rome declaration  the world has endorsed a set of guiding  principles for global preparedness  and preparedness is now at the center of  our union's action  and of course  the importance of this new endeavor  must also be reflected in its resources  therefore i have proposed an  unprecedented 50 billion euro budget  over seven years  for our health preparedness mission  our union  our member states  and of course the private sector  have a role to play and a contribution  to make  europe stands ready to contribute and  invest in pandemic preparedness  at home  and worldwide  ladies and gentlemen  for over 20 years now the world health  summit has been at the spare head of  international cooperation on health  and today finally there is broad  consensus  we must improve our preparedness and our  ability to respond to health crisis  so let's make it happen  i wish all of you  a very fruitful world health summit  thank you very much

